// seeds.memql
//
// The values epic memql#5414 decides by (issue #5416 and #5418).
//
// ONE GLOBAL SEED at the literal id `primary`: seed names are unique across
// the whole tree and v1:authoring:ladderPolicy's seed already holds the name
// `primary`, so this one is named feedbackPolicyPrimary and carries its id in
// its body. It materializes v1:work:feedbackPolicy:primary through
// createFeedbackPolicy, and every read (feedbackPolicyCurrent) pins that
// literal id.
//
// REFRESHED ON EVERY BOOT. The seed materializer re-asserts every global seed
// on every node at startup, and the fields a seed declares win, so these
// values are the ones the system applies after any restart. A write that does
// not change a value is skipped, so an unchanged seed costs one read per node
// per boot and appends no version.
//
// THE SAME VALUES LIVE IN GO EXACTLY ONCE, as
// component/work.DefaultFeedbackPolicy(), and only for a row that is absent or
// unreadable. Changing a value here changes the behaviour; changing it there
// changes nothing while this row exists.

/// The validator checks a goal run's answer before a person sees it, and two distinct goal
/// signatures make a construct reusable.
seed feedbackPolicy feedbackPolicyPrimary {
  id:                       "primary"
  validateAnswers:          true
  reusableAfterSignatures:  2
}
